[
    {
        "content": "<p>In Lean, many operators (e.g. &lt;) are defined in a type class, and each specific type (e.g. <code>Nat</code>) will have its own definition of the operator (e.g. <code>Nat.lt</code>).  I've found that if the goal involves an operator such as &lt;, tactics such as Aesop and <code>grind</code> will generally fail if the proof requires the underlying definition such as <code>Nat.lt</code>.  To help these tactics, how can I unfold the operator to go back to the original definition?</p>\n<p>Let's make this concrete via an example.  Here's a type <code>Color</code> with its own definition of &lt; :</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">less</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">color_less</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">less</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Here's a trivial goal that <code>grind</code> can solve:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">less</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">less</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However, if I pose it in terms of the operator &lt; then <code>grind</code> fails:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">less</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- `grind` failed</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I tried adding the type class instance, but that still fails:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">less</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">color_less</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- `grind` failed</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is there some tactic that will unfold the &lt;, yielding the goal <code>less (Color.red 2) (Color.red 3)</code> which grind can solve?  Alternatively, is there some option to <code>grind</code> or transparency mode that can help grind get past the &lt; operator?</p>\n<p>By the way, I'm aware that in this particular example other tactics will suffice, e.g.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">solve_by_elim</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- succeeds</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But I'm looking for an technique that will allow me to unfold an operator such as &lt; on harder problems in general.</p>",
        "id": 617282331,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1787079144
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This works, but perhaps makes <code>&lt;</code> unfold too aggressively:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">less</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simps</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">less</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lt_def</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">less</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 617288809,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1787081208
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>A simpler approach is just to write the four lemmas by hand that characterize <code>lt</code></p>",
        "id": 617288890,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1787081229
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There is also the (currently very rarely-used) <code>method_specs</code> attribute:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">less</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">method_specs</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">less</span>\n\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">instLTColor.lt_spec (x✝ x✝¹ : Color) :</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  (x✝ &lt; x✝¹) =</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">    match x✝, x✝¹ with</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">    | Color.red x, Color.red y =&gt; x &lt; y</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">    | Color.green x, Color.green y =&gt; x &lt; y</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">    | x, x_1 =&gt; False</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instLTColor</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lt_spec</span>\n\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">instLTColor.lt_spec_1 (x_2 y : ℕ) : (Color.red x_2 &lt; Color.red y) = (x_2 &lt; y)</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instLTColor</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lt_spec_1</span>\n\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">instLTColor.lt_spec_2 (x_2 y : ℕ) : (Color.green x_2 &lt; Color.green y) = (x_2 &lt; y)</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instLTColor</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lt_spec_2</span>\n\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">instLTColor.lt_spec_3 (x✝ x✝¹ : Color) (x_4 : ∀ (x y : ℕ), x✝ = Color.red x → x✝¹ = Color.red y → False)</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  (x_5 : ∀ (x y : ℕ), x✝ = Color.green x → x✝¹ = Color.green y → False) : (x✝ &lt; x✝¹) = False</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instLTColor</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lt_spec_3</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instLTColor</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lt_spec</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">less</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 617298032,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1787084425
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for the helpful suggestions.  They work, though I'm not sure I really understand what's going on here.  Eric, you wrote \"A simpler approach is just to write the four lemmas by hand that characterize <code>lt</code>\".   Are those the four lemmas that I see in Julia's reply?  Why would writing them be simpler than applying the <code>simps</code> attribute?</p>\n<p>When I write an instance declaration such as</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">less</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>does Lean automatically generate several lemmas?  If so, why is the <code>method_specs</code> attribute necessary to be able to access them?  Is any of this behavior documented anywhere, or must I just read the Lean source code to understand what's happening at this level?</p>",
        "id": 617305034,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1787086947
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Simpler in the sense that you do not need to import mathlib for them, and also in that you can consider <code>less</code> an implementatil detail and never see it again in proofs</p>",
        "id": 617305586,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1787087162
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The four lemmas are:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">red_lt_red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">red</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Iff</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Color</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">green_lt_green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">green</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><s